pre-message: video thumbnails from the UI's poster sidecar

Video was the one placeholder type left without a preview: core cannot decode
video frames, and its wasm runs in a Web Worker with no DOM, so the pixels can
only come from the UI.

Rather than invent a param for that, read the `<blob>-preview.jpg` sidecar
convention housekeeping already reserves (`is_file_in_use(.., "-preview.jpg")`,
the slot the mobile clients use for video thumbnails). It costs no `Param`, no
migration and no housekeeping change, and the poster is GCed exactly when the
video blob is — a param-referenced blob would instead be invisible to the scan,
which only extracts `Param::File` on msgs, and get deleted under a lingering
draft.

- blob: `VIDEO_PREVIEW_SUFFIX` + `video_preview_path()`; housekeeping now uses
  the constant, so renaming the convention is a compile error rather than a
  silently dead preview.
- `PostMsgMetadata::thumbnail()`: `Viewtype::Video` reads the sidecar when it
  exists, through the same `thumbnail_base64()` as every other type, so the
  128px/q40/20 KB budget stays enforced in one place. `path_exists` gates the
  read: videos from clients that write no sidecar are the normal case, not a
  warning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
